---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const updated = '21 September 2026';
---

<Layout title="Privacy Policy - Jim Paul De Jose">
  <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
  <p><em>Last updated: {updated}</em></p>

  <p>
    This policy covers the personal automation and integration tools described on the
    <a href="/automation">Automation &amp; Integrations</a> page. Those tools are built and
    operated by Jim Paul De Jose ("I", "me"). They are personal tools, not public services.
  </p>

  <h2>What this policy covers</h2>
  <p>
    Some of these tools connect to third-party services — including Google services — through APIs
    and OAuth, using my own accounts. This policy explains what data those connections access, how
    it is used, where it is stored, and who it is shared with. It applies to every tool listed on
    the Automation &amp; Integrations page, now and as that list grows.
  </p>

  <h2>Data accessed</h2>
  <p>
    Where a tool connects to a Google service, it requests only the permissions it needs to
    perform its function. Depending on the tool, that may include the ability to:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>send email on my behalf (Gmail);</li>
    <li>read and write calendar events (Google Calendar);</li>
    <li>read and write spreadsheet or file data (Google Sheets, Google Drive).</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    The exact permissions in use are shown on the Google consent screen when access is granted and
    in the tool's own configuration. A tool never requests more than the function it performs
    requires.
  </p>

  <h2>How data is used</h2>
  <p>
    Data is used solely to perform the function of the tool that requested it — for example, to
    send an email the tool has generated. It is not used for advertising, not used to build
    profiles, not sold, and not used to train or improve machine-learning models.
  </p>

  <h2>How data is stored and protected</h2>
  <p>
    OAuth tokens are stored encrypted on infrastructure I control. I do not retain the contents of
    emails, calendar entries, or files beyond what is needed to perform the requested action, and
    access is limited to me.
  </p>

  <h2>Sharing</h2>
  <p>
    Data is not shared with, sold to, or disclosed to any third party. It is not transferred to
    others except where strictly necessary to provide the tool's function, or where required by
    law.
  </p>

  <h2>Google Limited Use disclosure</h2>
  <p>
    Use of Google user data by these tools adheres to the
    <a href="https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google API Services User Data Policy</a>,
    including the Limited Use requirements.
  </p>

  <h2>Revoking access</h2>
  <p>
    Access can be revoked at any time at
    <a href="https://myaccount.google.com/permissions" target="_blank" rel="noopener">myaccount.google.com/permissions</a>.
    Revoking access stops the affected tool from working until it is authorised again.
  </p>

  <h2>Retention</h2>
  <p>
    Data held by a tool is kept only for as long as it is needed for that tool to function. Cached
    or archived data can be deleted on request and is purged automatically where a tool has a
    retention policy.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>
    This policy may be updated as the tools change or as new tools are added. The date at the top
    of this page shows when it last changed. The URL of this page stays the same.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>Questions about this policy: <a href="mailto:support@jimpaul.net">support@jimpaul.net</a>.</p>
</Layout>
